Package: ltsp-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         debootstrap,
         squashfs-tools,
         gettext-base,
         lsb-release,
         debconf-utils,
         openssh-client
Recommends: nbd-server,
            tftpd-hpa,
            dnsmasq | isc-dhcp-server,
            nfs-kernel-server,
            xinetd
Description: LTSP6 thin client server tools
 ltsp-build-client, ltsp-config, ltsp-chroot, ltsp-info and related
 server-side tools for building and managing LTSP (Linux Terminal
 Server Project) thin-client chroot images, plus the NBD root/swap
 servers used to serve them over the network.
 .
 This package also ships example configs and documentation for
 running an HAProxy + keepalived high-availability RDP load balancer
 in front of a pool of xrdp servers (see
 /usr/share/doc/ltsp-server/examples/).

Package: ltsp-client-core
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         initramfs-tools,
         udev,
         nbd-client,
         kbd,
         pciutils,
         xinit,
         x11-xserver-utils
Description: LTSP6 thin client core scripts and helpers
 Core client-side scripts, udev rules, initramfs-tools hooks and
 helper binaries (getltscfg, getltscfg-cluster, jetpipe, nbd-proxy,
 the localapps/remoteapps helpers) that make up the LTSP thin-client
 runtime environment. Intended to be installed inside an LTSP client
 chroot image built by ltsp-build-client, not on a regular desktop or
 server system.
